'The response correctly notes the absence of any specific mention of 'Sound Feedback' in the documents. While Documents 1 and 2 discuss sound settings, neither explicitly mentions the option of selecting 'Sound Feedback.'', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'a', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1b', '2b']}, {'explanation': 'This sentence accurately reflects information from Document 1, which lists various sound modes like Standard, Optimized, and Amplify that can be selected based on the content type or listening environment.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'b', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1b']}, {'explanation': 'This reflects the content of Document 2, which discusses the adjustment of expert settings, although it also accurately notes the absence of any specific mention of 'Sound Feedback'.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'c', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['2b']}]                                 []             True                                                                                                                                                          The response accurately reflects that the mentioned documents do not explicitly discuss the ability to select 'Sound Feedback.' While the response notes the types of settings and adjustments that can be made, such as selecting various sound modes and adjusting expert settings (from documents 1 and 2), none of the documents confirm nor deny if 'Sound Feedback' is a configurable option.                                    Document 1 is the most relevant as it mentions different sound modes and describes their selection process, though it does not specifically discuss 'Sound Feedback.' Document 2 is somewhat relevant as it involves configuring sound modes and expert settings, which could imply broader settings adjustment capabilities but does not explicitly mention 'Sound Feedback.' Document 0 holds no relevance to the question as it merely states that picture and sound settings can be adjusted without specifying whether 'Sound Feedback' is an option.                                                                                                      [1b, 1c, 2b]                                                                                                  [1b, 2b]                   NaN                        NaN                 NaN                      NaN             NaN                     NaN                NaN         0.428571           0.285714            0.666667\n2  emanual_423                                       What do I do if the channel is not found?                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [There Is a Problem with the Broadcast. When the TV has difficulties receiving broadcasts, these steps may help resolve the problem. The problem Try this! Weak or No Signal displayed in TV mode/ cannot find channel. The TV is not receiving all channels. There are no captions with digital channels. The picture is distorted. The picture quality is low. Select high definition (HD) channels or programs., Scanning for available channels. Settings Broadcasting Auto Program Try Now Do not use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box. If the TV has saved channels, Auto Program deletes the existing list, and then saves the newly scanned channels., Changing the broadcast signal. Live TV Channel List Press the right directional button on your remote control, move the focus to Air Cable , and then press the Select button. You do not need to use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             If the channel is not found, you should try scanning for available channels by selecting the option \"Settings\" then \"Broadcasting\" then \"Auto Program\" on your TV. Make sure not to use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box. Auto Program will delete the existing channel list and save the newly scanned channels.    gpt-3.5-turbo-0125  gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09  emanual_validation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              [[[0a, There Is a Problem with the Broadcast.], [0b, When the TV has difficulties receiving broadcasts, these steps may help resolve the problem.], [0c, The problem Try this!], [0d, Weak or No Signal displayed in TV mode/ cannot find channel.], [0e, The TV is not receiving all channels.], [0f, There are no captions with digital channels.], [0g, The picture is distorted.], [0h, The picture quality is low.], [0i, Select high definition (HD) channels or programs.]], [[1a, Scanning for available channels.], [1b, Settings Broadcasting Auto Program Try Now Do not use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box.], [1c, If the TV has saved channels, Auto Program deletes the existing list, and then saves the newly scanned channels.]], [[2a, Changing the broadcast signal.], [2b, Live TV Channel List Press the right directional button on your remote control, move the focus to Air Cable , and then press the Select button.], [2c, You do not need to use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box.]]]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               [[a, If the channel is not found, you should try scanning for available channels by selecting the option \"Settings\" then \"Broadcasting\" then \"Auto Program\" on your TV.], [b, Make sure not to use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box.], [c, Auto Program will delete the existing channel list and save the newly scanned channels.]]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             [{'explanation': 'The advice to use Settings > Broadcasting > Auto Program to scan for available channels is supported by sentence 1a combined with the reference in 1b.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'a', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1a', '1b']}, {'explanation': 'The caution to avoid using Auto Program when connected to a cable or satellite box is directly mentioned in both Documents 1 and 2, supporting this portion of the response completely.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'b', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1b', '2c']}, {'explanation': 'The response's claim that Auto Program deletes existing channels and saves new ones is explicitly supported by 1c.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'c', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1c']}]                                 []             True                                                                                                                                      The response as a whole is supported by the documents. Sentence 'a' is clearly supported by Document 1 which details using the Auto Program function to scan for channels. Sentence 'b' is also supported pertaining to when not to use Auto Program function as specified in both Document 1 and Document 2. Sentence 'c' accurately describes the effect of using Auto Program as stated in Document 1 (sentence 1c).                                                                                                                                                                       Document 1 contains the most relevant information regarding the question about what to do if a channel is not found, which suggests using the Auto Program feature as outlined in sentences 1a and 1c. Document 0 and Document 2 also contain useful information about channel-related troubleshooting and settings, but do not directly address the scenario of a channel not being found as explicitly as Document 1.                                                                                          [0d, 1a, 1b, 1c, 2b, 2c]                                                                                          [1a, 1b, 1c, 2c]                   NaN                        NaN                 NaN                      NaN             NaN                     NaN                NaN         0.400000           0.266667            0.666667\n3  emanual_529                                           Can I set the current time on the TV?                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [Setting the current time. Settings General System Manager Time Try Now You can set the Clock manually or automatically. Once the Clock is set, you can view the current time on the TV anytime. You must reset the clock in the following cases: The power cable is disconnected and then connected. The Clock Mode is changed from Manual Auto The TV is not connected to the Internet. No broadcast signals are received. Setting the clock automatically Settings General System Manager Time Clock Clock Mode Auto This function works only when the TV is connected to the Internet or is receiving digital broadcasts through a connected antenna. The accuracy of the time information received may differ with the channel and signal. If you get your TV signal from a cable broadcast receiver/set-top box or a satellite receiver/satellite set-top box connected to an HDMI or Component port, you must set the current time manually.  Adjusting the clock for DST and time zone Settings General System Manager Time Clock Sets the right time by setting Daylight Savings Time (DST) and your local time zone. Time Zone Selects your time zone. This function is only available when the Clock Mode is set to Auto DST Automatically adjusts for Daylight Saving Time (DST). This function is only available when the Clock Mode is set to Auto Changing the current time Settings General System Manager Time Clock Time Offset Time Offset adjusts the time through a network connection. This function is only available if Clock Mode is set to Auto and the TV is connected to the Internet though a local area network. Time Offset adjusts the time if the TV fails to receive time information through normal digital broadcast signals. Setting the clock manually Settings General System Manager Time Clock Clock Mode Manual When Clock Mode is set to Manual , you can directly enter the current time. Select the Date and Time by using the directional buttons on the remote control., Using the timers. Using the sleep timer Settings General System Manager Time Sleep Timer You can use this function to automatically shut off the TV after a pre-set period of time. You can set the sleep timer for up to 180 minutes after which it will turn off the TV. Turning off the TV using the off timer Settings General System Manager Time Off Timer You can set Off Timer to shut off the TV automatically at a specific time. Off Timer is only available if the Clock has been set. , Setting Up a Schedule Viewing. Configure the TV to show a specific channel or program at a specific time and date. The icon appears next to programs that have been configured for a schedule viewing. To set up a schedule viewing, you must first set the TV's clock ( Settings General System Manager Time Clock Setting up a schedule viewing The Guide Screen On the Guide screen, select a program you would like to view, and then press and hold the Select button. Select Schedule Viewing on the pop-up menu that appears. The Program Info Screen Press the Select button while watching the TV. The Program Info window appears. Select a broadcast scheduled program by using the left or right directional buttons, and then press the Select button. You can schedule watching the program by selecting Schedule Viewing ]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      Yes, you can set the current time on the TV either manually or automatically.    gpt-3.5-turbo-0125  gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09  emanual_validation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         