 Sound Output menu.], [0g, ( Settings Sound Sound Output An unusual noise coming from a connected audio device while you are using it may indicate a problem with the audio device itself.], [0h, If this occurs, ask for assistance from the audio device's manufacturer.], [0i, Digital audio is only available with 5.1 channel broadcasts.]], [[1a, Connecting with a digital audio (optical) cable.]], [[2a, Audio Input and Output Connections.], [2b, Make the correct audio connections between your TV and your external devices.], [2c, For more information about how to select external speakers, refer to]]]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             [[a, To get better audio quality, it is recommended to use an AV receiver when connecting audio devices.], [b, When connecting an external audio device using an optical cable, ensure that you turn on the external audio device before connecting the optical cable.], [c, By doing so, the Sound Output setting will be automatically changed to the connected device.], [d, Additionally, you can manually change the Sound Output setting by using the Quick Settings screen or the Settings screen to select Audio Out/Optical on the Sound Output menu.], [e, If you encounter unusual noises coming from a connected audio device, it may indicate a problem with the audio device itself, and you should seek assistance from the manufacturer.], [f, Additionally, digital audio is only available with 5.1 channel broadcasts.]]                                                                               