ecifically on the Learn TV Remote page.], [1q, Press a button on the remote.], [1r, The name and function of the button are heard.], [1s, When you have finished and want to exit the e-Manual, press the button twice to go to the previous page.], [1t, Accessing the main accessibility menu to change Voice Guide settings You can also go to an accessibility menu from the TV settings menu.], [1u, This provides more options, for example, to change the speed of Voice Guide.], [1v, The TV will not verbalize this menu unless Voice Guide is already turned on.], [1w, Press the button.], [1x, Press the left directional button until you reach Settings Press Select and a menu will open.], [1y, Press the down directional button to reach General , and then press Select to open this menu.], [1z, Use the directional buttons to go to the Accessibility menu, and then press Select to open this menu.], [1aa, The menu will appear with Voice Guide Settings being the first menu.], [1ab, Highlight Voice Guide Settings , and then press Select.], [1ac, A menu appears with the options to change Voice Guide and Volume Speed Pitch Select the menu using the directional buttons, and then press Select.]], [[2a, Enabling voice guides for the visually impaired.], [2b, Settings General Accessibility Voice Guide Settings Try Now You can activate voice guides that describe the menu options aloud to aid the visually impaired.], [2c, To activate this function, set Voice Guide .], [2d, With Voice Guide on, the TV provides voice guides for channel change, volume adjust, information on current and upcoming programs, schedule viewing, other TV functions, and various content in the Internet , and in Search You can go to Voice Guide , and then press the Select button to turn the function on or off.], [2e, The Voice Guide is provided in the language that is specified on the Language screen.], [2f, However, some languages are not supported by Voice Guide even though they are listed in the Language screen.], [2g, English is always supported.], [2h, For more information about the TV language settings, refer to the menu Changing the volume, speed, and pitch of the Voice Guide You can configure the volume, speed, and pitch of the voice guide.]]]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      [[a, To enable audio for the video description function, you need to follow these steps: 1.], [b, Press and hold the VOL button on the remote to bring up the Accessibility Shortcuts menu. 2.], [c, Use the up or down directional buttons on the remote to highlight the Video Description option. 3.], [d, Press the Select button on the remote to turn Video Description on or off. 4.], [e, Close the menu either by pressing on the remote or by highlighting Close with the right directional button and then pressing the Select button.], [f, By following these steps, you can activate the audio guide that provides an audio description of video scenes for the visually impaired.]]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             [{'explanation': 'The overall introduction is generically supported without reference to specific sentences.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'a', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['general']}, {'explanation': 'This sentence is supported by Document 1, which explains how to access the Accessibility Shortcuts menu using the VOL button.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'b', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1g']}, {'explanation': 'This sentence is supported by Document 1, stating which buttons on the remote to use to highlight the Video Description option.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'c', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1i']}, {'explanation': 'The action specified in this sentence is validated by a sentence in Document 1 describing how to toggle the Video Description feature on and off.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'd', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1j']}, {'explanation': 'This sentence is supported by Document 1, which provides details on how to close the menu after making selections.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'e', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['1k']}, {'explanation': 'Supported by Document 0b, which explains what activating video description enables (audio guide that describes scenes for visually impaired).', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'f', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0b']}]                                 []             True                                                                                                                                                                                                                     The response thoroughly details the procedure to enable audio for the video description function, and each step is supported by sentences in Document 1. All the operations outlined in the response, such as using the VOL button, navigating through the menu, and selecting the Video Description option are described in Document 1.                                                       Document 1 contains the most relevant and detailed information for the question about enabling audio for video description. It outlines the steps required to activate the Video Description function via remote control commands, which is directly related to the query. Document 0 mentions the availability of the audio description feature for the visually impaired but does not provide detailed activation steps. Document 2, while discussing voice guide features, does not address the video description function directly.                                                                                      [0b, 0c, 1g, 1h, 1i, 1j, 1k]                                                                                  [0b, 1g, 1h, 1i, 1j, 1k]                   NaN                        NaN                 NaN                      NaN             NaN                     NaN                NaN         0.175000           0.150000            0.857143\n8  emanual_567                      I want to update the TV automatically. How can I do that ?                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [Updating the TV automatically. Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV's software update itself automatically while you are watching the TV. When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on. If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically. If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off. This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently. This function requires an Internet connection. , Updating the TV automatically. Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV update its software automatically while you are watching the TV. When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on. If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically. If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off. This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently. This function requires an Internet connection. , Updating the TV's software to the latest version. DO NOT turn off the TV's power until the update is complete. The TV will turn off and on automatically after completing the software update. Video and audio settings will be reset to their defaults after a software update. Updating through the Internet Settings Support Software Update Update Now Try Now Updating from the Internet requires an active Internet connection. Updating through a USB device Settings Support Software Update Update Now After downloading the update file from the Samsung website and storing it on a USB device, connect the USB device to the TV to update. To update using a USB flash drive, download the update package from Samsung.com to your computer. Then, save the update package in the USB device's top-level folder. Otherwise, the TV will not be able to locate the update package.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            To update the TV automatically, ensure that the TV is connected to the Internet. Then, go to Settings, navigate to Support, select Software Update, and then choose Auto Update. If Auto Update is not already enabled, you can use the Select button to turn it on. Once enabled, the TV's software will update itself automatically in the background while you are watching TV. The update will be applied the next time the TV is turned on. Just make sure to agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions for Auto Update to work.    gpt-3.5-turbo-0125  gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09  emanual_validation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           