ime if another network function is running concurrently.], [1g, This function requires an Internet connection.]], [[2a, Updating the TV's software to the latest version.], [2b, DO NOT turn off the TV's power until the update is complete.], [2c, The TV will turn off and on automatically after completing the software update.], [2d, Video and audio settings will be reset to their defaults after a software update.], [2e, Updating through the Internet Settings Support Software Update Update Now Try Now Updating from the Internet requires an active Internet connection.], [2f, Updating through a USB device Settings Support Software Update Update Now After downloading the update file from the Samsung website and storing it on a USB device, connect the USB device to the TV to update.], [2g, To update using a USB flash drive, download the update package from Samsung.com to your computer.], [2h, Then, save the update package in the USB device's top-level folder.], [2i, Otherwise, the TV will not be able to locate the update package.]]]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [[a, To update the TV automatically, ensure that the TV is connected to the Internet.], [b, Then, go to Settings, navigate to Support, select Software Update, and then choose Auto Update.], [c, If Auto Update is not already enabled, you can use the Select button to turn it on.], [d, Once enabled, the TV's software will update itself automatically in the background while you are watching TV.], [e, The update will be applied the next time the TV is turned on.], [f, Just make sure to agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions for Auto Update to work.]]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              [{'explanation': 'The sentence is supported as both Document 0 and Document 1 specify that automating updates requires the TV to be connected to the internet.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'a', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0b', '1b']}, {'explanation': 'The directive steps provided in the response are outlined almost verbatim in Document 0 and 1, which describe navigating through Settings to enable Auto Update.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'b', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0b', '1b']}, {'explanation': 'Document 0 and Document 1 both mention the use of the Select button to turn the Auto Update function on or off, which supports the action described in the response.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'c', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0e', '1e']}, {'explanation': 'Both Document 0 and Document 1 explicitly state that once Auto Update is enabled, the TV updates itself automatically in the background while the TV is being watched.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'd', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0b', '1b']}, {'explanation': 'This sentence is supported by text from Document 0 and Document 1, which both mention that the software update, once downloaded, is applied the next time the TV is powered on.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'e', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0c', '1c']}, {'explanation': 'The requirement to agree to Smart Hub terms and conditions for Auto Update to function is mentioned in Document 0 and Document 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'f', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0d', '1d']}]                                 []             True  The response accurately reflects the information contained in Documents 0 and 1 on how to set up and enable automatic updates on a TV connected to the internet. The step-by-step instructions in the response match those in the documents, including enabling the auto update feature, requirements to be connected to the internet, using the settings menu to navigate to it, and the applicability of software updates upon the next TV turn-on. The information about agreeing to Smart Hub terms to ensure auto update activation is also supported.                                               Documents 0 and 1 provide almost identical information relating to setting up and enabling automatic TV updates via an internet connection. They outline steps within TV settings to enable this feature along with dependencies such as internet connection and agreeing to the Smart Hub terms. Document 2, while it does discuss updating the TV's software, it focuses on methods like updates via a USB device rather than automatic updates over the internet, making it less relevant to answering the question about automatic updates.                                                                                          [0b, 0d, 0e, 1b, 1d, 1e]                                                                          [0b, 0c, 0d, 0e, 1b, 1c, 1d, 1e]                   NaN                        NaN                 NaN                      NaN             NaN                     NaN                NaN         0.260870           0.347826            1.000000\n9  emanual_275                                             What are the precautions for bixby?  [Read Before Using Bixby. Precautions for Bixby The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area. If the language set differs from the language of your country, some features are not available. Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet. Even if the TV is connected to the Internet, there may be no response due to a Bixby server error. The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated. Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone. Symbols including and special characters are not supported. Consequently, if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly. Searched results may not provide complete results. You may be required to pay for some apps. Consequently, you may encounter a service application or contract. To change the current channel by saying channel names as voice commands, you must finish Set Up Your Service Provider . If Set Up Your Service Provider is not completed, you can complete it using the following menu. Settings General Start Setup Try Now To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data. To use the Bixby function, you must: Agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use Agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service. Consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service. Requirements for using Bixby The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise). The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB. , Read Before Using Bixby. Precautions for Bixby The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area. If the language set differs from the language of your country, some features are not available. Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet. Even if the TV is connected to the Internet, there may be no response due to a Bixby server error. The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated. Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone. Symbols including and special characters are not supported. Consequently, if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly. Searched results may not provide complete results. You may be required to pay for some apps. Consequently, you may encounter a service application or contract. To change the current channel by saying channel names as voice commands, you must finish Set Up Your Service Provider . If Set Up Your Service Provider is not completed, you can complete it using the following menu. Settings General Start Setup Try Now To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data. To use the Bixby function, you must: Agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use Agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service. Consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service. Requirements for using Bixby The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise). The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB. , Learning about My Bixby. The image on your TV may differ from the image above depending on the model and geographical area. Samsung Account Go to the Samsung Account screen to create a new account or sign out of your account. If you are signed out of your Samsung account, select Sign In to log in. Settings You can change the voice responses and the voice style of Bixby You can also select a music service provider in the Default music service provider tab. The Default music service provider tab may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area. User information and the experience points (XP) guide You can see user information and the experience points (XP) that you can get from using Bixby You must be signed in to your Samsung account to view the user information and the experience points (XP). This function may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area. Bixby guide You can learn the voice commands that let you use Bixby in various situations. Use the directional buttons to move to the desired command, and then press the Select button. You can operate the TV with various voice commands. To view a tutorial on Bixby , use the directional buttons to move to the bottom, and then select the View Tutorial item. My Bixby ]  1. The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area.\\n2. Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet.\\n3. The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated.\\n4. Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone.\\n5. Symbols including and special characters are not supported, so if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly.\\n6. Searched results may not provide complete results, and you may be required to pay for some apps.\\n7. To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data.\\n8. To use the Bixby function, you must agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use, agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service, and consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service.\\n9. The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise). The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB.    gpt-3.5-turbo-0125  gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09  emanual_validation  [[[0a, Read Before Using Bixby.], [0b, Precautions for Bixby The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area.], [0c, If the language set differs from the language of your country, some features are not available.], [0d, Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet.], [0e, Even if the TV is connected to the Internet, there may be no response due to a Bixby server error.], [0f, The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated.], [0g, Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone.], [0h, Symbols including and special characters are not supported.], [0i, Consequently, if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly.], [0j, Searched results may not provide complete results.], [0k, You may be required to pay for some apps.], [0l, Consequently, you may encounter a service application or contract.], [0m, To change the current channel by saying channel names as voice commands, you must finish Set Up Your Service Provider .], [0n, If Set Up Your Service Provider is not completed, you can complete it using the following menu.], [0o, Settings General Start Setup Try Now To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data.], [0p, To use the Bixby function, you must: Agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use Agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service.], [0q, Consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service.], [0r, Requirements for using Bixby The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise).], [0s, The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB.]], [[1a, Read Before Using Bixby.], [1b, Precautions for Bixby The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area.], [1c, If the language set differs from the language of your country, some features are not available.], [1d, Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet.], [1e, Even if the TV is connected to the Internet, there may be no response due to a Bixby server error.], [1f, The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated.], [1g, Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone.], [1h, Symbols including and special characters are not supported.], [1i, Consequently, if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly.], [1j, Searched results may not provide complete results.], [1k, You may be required to pay for some apps.], [1l, Consequently, you may encounter a service application or contract.], [1m, To change the current channel by saying channel names as voice commands, you must finish Set Up Your Service Provider .], [1n, If Set Up Your Service Provider is not completed, you can complete it using the following menu.], [1o, Settings General Start Setup Try Now To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data.], [1p, To use the Bixby function, you must: Agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use Agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service.], [1q, Consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service.], [1r, Requirements for using Bixby The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise).], [1s, The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB.]], [[2a, Learning about My Bixby.], [2b, The image on your TV may differ from the image above depending on the model and geographical area.], [2c, Samsung Account Go to the Samsung Account screen to create a new account or sign out of your account.], [2d, If you are signed out of your Samsung account, select Sign In to log in.], [2e, Settings You can change the voice responses and the voice style of Bixby You can also select a music service provider in the Default music service provider tab.], [2f, The Default music service provider tab may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area.], [2g, User information and the experience points (XP) guide You can see user information and the experience points (XP) that you can get from using Bixby You must be signed in to your Samsung account to view the user information and the experience points (XP).], [2h, This function may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area.], [2i, Bixby guide You can learn the voice commands that let you use Bixby in various situations.], [2j, Use the directional buttons to move to the desired command, and then press the Select button.], [2k, You can operate the TV with various voice commands.], [2l, To view a tutorial on Bixby , use the directional buttons to move to the bottom, and then select the View Tutorial item. My Bixby]]]  [[a, 1. The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area. 2.], [b, Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet. 3.], [c, The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated. 4.], [d, Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone. 5.], [e, Symbols including and special characters are not supported, so if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly. 6.], [f, Searched results may not provide complete results, and you may be required to pay for some apps. 7.], [g, To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data. 8.], [h, To use the Bixby function, you must agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use, agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service, and consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service. 9.], [i, The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise).], [j, The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB.]]  [{'explanation': 'This information about language and features varying by geographical area is supported directly by Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'a', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0b', '1b']}, {'explanation': 'This statement about Bixby's availability with an internet connection is found in Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'b', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0d', '1d']}, {'explanation': 'The potential for changing specifications with an update is mentioned in Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'c', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0f', '1f']}, {'explanation': 'The availability of Bixby on supported TVs with specific remotes is noted in Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'd', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0g', '1g']}, {'explanation': 'The issue with unsupported symbols and special characters influencing functionality is mentioned in Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'e', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0h', '0i', '1h', '1i']}, {'explanation': 'Issues with incomplete search results and potential app charges are covered in Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'f', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0j', '0k', '1j', '1k']}, {'explanation': 'The requirement for user consent to collect and use voice data for certain functions is documented in Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'g', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0o', '1o']}, {'explanation': 'The necessity for agreeing to terms of use and privacy terms to utilize Bixby is supported by information in Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'h', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0p', '0q', '1p', '1q']}, {'explanation': 'This description of how voice interaction rates can vary is supported by Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'i', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0r', '1r']}, {'explanation': 'The details about optimal volume levels for voice commands are found in Documents 0 and 1.', 'fully_supported': None, 'response_sentence_key': 'j', 'supporting_sentence_keys': ['0s', '1s']}]                                 []             True                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               The response is fully supported by the documents. Each point made in the response regarding the precautions and requirements for using Bixby correlates directly with specific sentences in Documents 0 and 1, which detail these precautions comprehensively.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             Document 0 and Document 1 contain useful information for answering the question about Bixby's precautions as they list specific precautions and usage constraints related to Bixby. Document 2, however, focuses more on additional features and user guide content that does not directly answer the question about precautions.  [0b, 0d, 0f, 0g, 0h, 0i, 0j, 0k, 0l, 0o, 0p, 0q, 0r, 0s, 1b, 1d, 1f, 1g, 1h, 1i, 1j, 1k, 1l, 1o, 1p, 1q, 1r, 1s]  [0b, 0d, 0f, 0g, 0h, 0i, 0j, 0k, 0o, 0p, 0q, 0r, 0s, 1b, 1d, 1f, 1g, 1h, 1i, 1j, 1k, 1o, 1p, 1q, 1r, 1s]                   NaN                        NaN                 NaN                      NaN             NaN                     NaN                NaN         0.560000           0.520000            0.928571"}
{"asctime": "2026-06-27 13:47:04,248", "levelname": "DEBUG", "name": "real_world_rag", "message": "                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     documents                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        documents_sentences\n0                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      [Smart Hub. View descriptions of Smart Hub's basic functions. From Smart Hub, you can use the Internet search function, install and use various apps, view photos and videos, or listen to music stored on external storage devices, and perform more functions. Some Smart Hub services are paid services. To use Smart Hub , the TV must be connected to the Internet. Some Smart Hub features may not be supported depending on the service provider, language, or geographical area. Smart Hub service outages can be caused by disruptions in your Internet service. You can view the entire text of the Terms & Policy document by navigating to Settings Support Terms & Policy Try Now If you want to stop using Smart Hub , you can cancel the agreement. To cancel the Smart Hub service agreement, select Reset Smart Hub Settings Support Self Diagnosis Reset Smart Hub ). Note that accepting and maintaining the Smart Hub service agreement is required if you want to use Smart Hub and other features and functions on your TV. , Smart Hub. After pressing the button on your remote control, you can surf the web and download apps with Smart Hub. Some Smart Hub services are for pay services. To use Smart Hub , the TV must be connected to the Internet. Some Smart Hub features may not be supported depending on the service provider, language, or geographical area. Smart Hub service outages can be caused by disruptions to your Internet service. You can view the entire text of the Terms & Policy by navigating to Settings Support Terms & Policy If you want to stop using Smart Hub , you can cancel the agreement. To cancel the Smart Hub service agreement, select Reset Smart Hub Settings Support Self Diagnosis Reset Smart Hub ). Note that accepting and maintaining the Smart Hub service agreement is required if you want to use Smart Hub and other features and functions on your TV. Press the button on your remote. This will bring up a display with 2 rows. Try moving the focus to Live TV another item on the bottom row. The options on the top row change depending on the item selected in the bottom row. The buttons to the right of Live TV provide quick access to apps such as Netflix and Amazon . Currently, many of these apps are not accessible with Voice Guide. Use the left and right directional buttons to move between a menu or apps on a row and the up and down directional buttons to move between rows. Press Select to access a menu or apps. When you open Smart Hub , you will be on Live TV TV PLUS . Press the up directional button to move to the top row. You will be on the Guide item. The items in this row are: Guide : Select to go to the Program Guide where you can view the program schedules for multiple channels. Channel List : Select to open the channel list to view and move to programs that are being broadcast on other channels. Schedule Manager Recordings : You can go to the Schedule Manager Recording & Schedule Manager screen. This function may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area. To the right of Schedule Manager Recordings , you can see the programs you viewed most recently and the programs that are currently broadcasting on other channels. To go to one of those channels, move to it, and then press the Select button. , Smart Features. You can enjoy various apps with Smart Hub.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              [[[0a, Smart Hub. View descriptions of Smart Hub's basic functions.], [0b, From Smart Hub, you can use the Internet search function, install and use various apps, view photos and videos, or listen to music stored on external storage devices, and perform more functions.], [0c, Some Smart Hub services are paid services.], [0d, To use Smart Hub , the TV must be connected to the Internet.], [0e, Some Smart Hub features may not be supported depending on the service provider, language, or geographical area.], [0f, Smart Hub service outages can be caused by disruptions in your Internet service.], [0g, You can view the entire text of the Terms & Policy document by navigating to Settings Support Terms & Policy Try Now If you want to stop using Smart Hub , you can cancel the agreement.], [0h, To cancel the Smart Hub service agreement, select Reset Smart Hub Settings Support Self Diagnosis Reset Smart Hub ).], [0i, Note that accepting and maintaining the Smart Hub service agreement is required if you want to use Smart Hub and other features and functions on your TV.]], [[1a, Smart Hub. After pressing the button on your remote control, you can surf the web and download apps with Smart Hub.], [1b, Some Smart Hub services are for pay services.], [1c, To use Smart Hub , the TV must be connected to the Internet.], [1d, Some Smart Hub features may not be supported depending on the service provider, language, or geographical area.], [1e, Smart Hub service outages can be caused by disruptions to your Internet service.], [1f, You can view the entire text of the Terms & Policy by navigating to Settings Support Terms & Policy If you want to stop using Smart Hub , you can cancel the agreement.], [1g, To cancel the Smart Hub service agreement, select Reset Smart Hub Settings Support Self Diagnosis Reset Smart Hub ).], [1h, Note that accepting and maintaining the Smart Hub service agreement is required if you want to use Smart Hub and other features and functions on your TV.], [1i, Press the button on your remote.], [1j, This will bring up a display with 2 rows.], [1k, Try moving the focus to Live TV another item on the bottom row.], [1l, The options on the top row change depending on the item selected in the bottom row.], [1m, The buttons to the right of Live TV provide quick access to apps such as Netflix and Amazon .], [1n, Currently, many of these apps are not accessible with Voice Guide.], [1o, Use the left and right directional buttons to move between a menu or apps on a row and the up and down directional buttons to move between rows.], [1p, Press Select to access a menu or apps.], [1q, When you open Smart Hub , you will be on Live TV TV PLUS .], [1r, Press the up directional button to move to the top row.], [1s, You will be on the Guide item.], [1t, The items in this row are: Guide : Select to go to the Program Guide where you can view the program schedules for multiple channels.], [1u, Channel List : Select to open the channel list to view and move to programs that are being broadcast on other channels.], [1v, Schedule Manager Recordings : You can go to the Schedule Manager Recording & Schedule Manager screen.], [1w, This function may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area.], [1x, To the right of Schedule Manager Recordings , you can see the programs you viewed most recently and the programs that are currently broadcasting on other channels.], [1y, To go to one of those channels, move to it, and then press the Select button.]], [[2a, Smart Features. You can enjoy various apps with Smart Hub.]]]\n1                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               [Picture and Sound. You can change the settings for the picture and the sound according to your preference., Choosing a sound mode. Settings Sound Sound Mode Try Now You can select a favorite sound mode suitable for the content type or the listening environment. Standard Optimized Amplify This function may not be supported depending on the model., Configuring a Sound Mode and Expert Settings. Change the Sound Mode and adjust Expert Settings.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         [[[0a, Picture and Sound.], [0b, You can change the settings for the picture and the sound according to your preference.]], [[1a, Choosing a sound mode.], [1b, Settings Sound Sound Mode Try Now You can select a favorite sound mode suitable for the content type or the listening environment.], [1c, Standard Optimized Amplify This function may not be supported depending on the model.]], [[2a, Configuring a Sound Mode and Expert Settings.], [2b, Change the Sound Mode and adjust Expert Settings.]]]\n2                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [There Is a Problem with the Broadcast. When the TV has difficulties receiving broadcasts, these steps may help resolve the problem. The problem Try this! Weak or No Signal displayed in TV mode/ cannot find channel. The TV is not receiving all channels. There are no captions with digital channels. The picture is distorted. The picture quality is low. Select high definition (HD) channels or programs., Scanning for available channels. Settings Broadcasting Auto Program Try Now Do not use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box. If the TV has saved channels, Auto Program deletes the existing list, and then saves the newly scanned channels., Changing the broadcast signal. Live TV Channel List Press the right directional button on your remote control, move the focus to Air Cable , and then press the Select button. You do not need to use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              [[[0a, There Is a Problem with the Broadcast.], [0b, When the TV has difficulties receiving broadcasts, these steps may help resolve the problem.], [0c, The problem Try this!], [0d, Weak or No Signal displayed in TV mode/ cannot find channel.], [0e, The TV is not receiving all channels.], [0f, There are no captions with digital channels.], [0g, The picture is distorted.], [0h, The picture quality is low.], [0i, Select high definition (HD) channels or programs.]], [[1a, Scanning for available channels.], [1b, Settings Broadcasting Auto Program Try Now Do not use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box.], [1c, If the TV has saved channels, Auto Program deletes the existing list, and then saves the newly scanned channels.]], [[2a, Changing the broadcast signal.], [2b, Live TV Channel List Press the right directional button on your remote control, move the focus to Air Cable , and then press the Select button.], [2c, You do not need to use this function if your TV is connected to a cable box or satellite box.]]]\n3                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [Setting the current time. Settings General System Manager Time Try Now You can set the Clock manually or automatically. Once the Clock is set, you can view the current time on the TV anytime. You must reset the clock in the following cases: The power cable is disconnected and then connected. The Clock Mode is changed from Manual Auto The TV is not connected to the Internet. No broadcast signals are received. Setting the clock automatically Settings General System Manager Time Clock Clock Mode Auto This function works only when the TV is connected to the Internet or is receiving digital broadcasts through a connected antenna. The accuracy of the time information received may differ with the channel and signal. If you get your TV signal from a cable broadcast receiver/set-top box or a satellite receiver/satellite set-top box connected to an HDMI or Component port, you must set the current time manually.  Adjusting the clock for DST and time zone Settings General System Manager Time Clock Sets the right time by setting Daylight Savings Time (DST) and your local time zone. Time Zone Selects your time zone. This function is only available when the Clock Mode is set to Auto DST Automatically adjusts for Daylight Saving Time (DST). This function is only available when the Clock Mode is set to Auto Changing the current time Settings General System Manager Time Clock Time Offset Time Offset adjusts the time through a network connection. This function is only available if Clock Mode is set to Auto and the TV is connected to the Internet though a local area network. Time Offset adjusts the time if the TV fails to receive time information through normal digital broadcast signals. Setting the clock manually Settings General System Manager Time Clock Clock Mode Manual When Clock Mode is set to Manual , you can directly enter the current time. Select the Date and Time by using the directional buttons on the remote control., Using the timers. Using the sleep timer Settings General System Manager Time Sleep Timer You can use this function to automatically shut off the TV after a pre-set period of time. You can set the sleep timer for up to 180 minutes after which it will turn off the TV. Turning off the TV using the off timer Settings General System Manager Time Off Timer You can set Off Timer to shut off the TV automatically at a specific time. Off Timer is only available if the Clock has been set. , Setting Up a Schedule Viewing. Configure the TV to show a specific channel or program at a specific time and date. The icon appears next to programs that have been configured for a schedule viewing. To set up a schedule viewing, you must first set the TV's clock ( Settings General System Manager Time Clock Setting up a schedule viewing The Guide Screen On the Guide screen, select a program you would like to view, and then press and hold the Select button. Select Schedule Viewing on the pop-up menu that appears. The Program Info Screen Press the Select button while watching the TV. The Program Info window appears. Select a broadcast scheduled program by using the left or right directional buttons, and then press the Select button. You can schedule watching the program by selecting Schedule Viewing ]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [[[0a, Setting the current time.], [0b, Settings General System Manager Time Try Now You can set the Clock manually or automatically.], [0c, Once the Clock is set, you can view the current time on the TV anytime.], [0d, You must reset the clock in the following cases: The power cable is disconnected and then connected.], [0e, The Clock Mode is changed from Manual Auto The TV is not connected to the Internet.], [0f, No broadcast signals are received.], [0g, Setting the clock automatically Settings General System Manager Time Clock Clock Mode Auto This function works only when the TV is connected to the Internet or is receiving digital broadcasts through a connected antenna.], [0h, The accuracy of the time information received may differ with the channel and signal.], [0i, If you get your TV signal from a cable broadcast receiver/set-top box or a satellite receiver/satellite set-top box connected to an HDMI or Component port, you must set the current time manually.], [0j, Adjusting the clock for DST and time zone Settings General System Manager Time Clock Sets the right time by setting Daylight Savings Time (DST) and your local time zone.], [0k, Time Zone Selects your time zone.], [0l, This function is only available when the Clock Mode is set to Auto DST Automatically adjusts for Daylight Saving Time (DST).], [0m, This function is only available when the Clock Mode is set to Auto Changing the current time Settings General System Manager Time Clock Time Offset Time Offset adjusts the time through a network connection.], [0n, This function is only available if Clock Mode is set to Auto and the TV is connected to the Internet though a local area network.], [0o, Time Offset adjusts the time if the TV fails to receive time information through normal digital broadcast signals.], [0p, Setting the clock manually Settings General System Manager Time Clock Clock Mode Manual When Clock Mode is set to Manual , you can directly enter the current time.], [0q, Select the Date and Time by using the directional buttons on the remote control.]], [[1a, Using the timers.], [1b, Using the sleep timer Settings General System Manager Time Sleep Timer You can use this function to automatically shut off the TV after a pre-set period of time.], [1c, You can set the sleep timer for up to 180 minutes after which it will turn off the TV.], [1d, Turning off the TV using the off timer Settings General System Manager Time Off Timer You can set Off Timer to shut off the TV automatically at a specific time.], [1e, Off Timer is only available if the Clock has been set.]], [[2a, Setting Up a Schedule Viewing.], [2b, Configure the TV to show a specific channel or program at a specific time and date.], [2c, The icon appears next to programs that have been configured for a schedule viewing.], [2d, To set up a schedule viewing, you must first set the TV's clock ( Settings General System Manager Time Clock Setting up a schedule viewing The Guide Screen On the Guide screen, select a program you would like to view, and then press and hold the Select button.], [2e, Select Schedule Viewing on the pop-up menu that appears.], [2f, The Program Info Screen Press the Select button while watching the TV.], [2g, The Program Info window appears.], [2h, Select a broadcast scheduled program by using the left or right directional buttons, and then press the Select button.], [2i, You can schedule watching the program by selecting Schedule Viewing]]]\n4                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     [Connecting to the TV via the SmartThings app. Turn on the TV. Start the SmartThings app on your mobile device. Tap Add Device on the dashboard of the SmartThings app. Connectable TVs are searched for. From the search results, select the model of your TV. Enter the PIN number displayed on the TV screen. Once the TV is registered with your Samsung account, you can use the SmartThings app to control the TV. If your TV is not found on your mobile device, turn both of them off and on, and then try again. If you have more than one TV, you can easily select the TV you want by setting different TV names at Settings General System Manager Device Name , Connecting Your Mobile Device. Connect your mobile device to the TV on the same network to control the TV with the mobile device or enjoy the content of the mobile device on the TV. Use the SmartThings app on your mobile device to quickly and easily connect to the TV and control its main settings. In addition, you can remotely check and control the statuses of various devices such as Samsung smart devices, home appliances, and speakers registered to the server. Make sure that your TV supports SmartThings. You can check this with the Supported Device menu in the SmartThings app. To use the SmartThings app, you must be signed in to your Samsung account on the TV. This function may not be supported depending on the TV model or mobile device. The supported functions may differ depending on the version of the SmartThings app. You can install the SmartThings app from App Store or Google Play Store., Managing Mobile Devices. Settings General External Device Manager Device Connect Manager Try Now Access Notification Set whether to display a notification when a mobile device attempts to connect to the TV. Device List View, edit, or remove a list of mobile devices registered to the TV.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                [[[0a, Connecting to the TV via the SmartThings app.], [0b, Turn on the TV.], [0c, Start the SmartThings app on your mobile device.], [0d, Tap Add Device on the dashboard of the SmartThings app.], [0e, Connectable TVs are searched for.], [0f, From the search results, select the model of your TV.], [0g, Enter the PIN number displayed on the TV screen.], [0h, Once the TV is registered with your Samsung account, you can use the SmartThings app to control the TV.], [0i, If your TV is not found on your mobile device, turn both of them off and on, and then try again.], [0j, If you have more than one TV, you can easily select the TV you want by setting different TV names at Settings General System Manager Device Name]], [[1a, Connecting Your Mobile Device.], [1b, Connect your mobile device to the TV on the same network to control the TV with the mobile device or enjoy the content of the mobile device on the TV.], [1c, Use the SmartThings app on your mobile device to quickly and easily connect to the TV and control its main settings.], [1d, In addition, you can remotely check and control the statuses of various devices such as Samsung smart devices, home appliances, and speakers registered to the server.], [1e, Make sure that your TV supports SmartThings.], [1f, You can check this with the Supported Device menu in the SmartThings app.], [1g, To use the SmartThings app, you must be signed in to your Samsung account on the TV.], [1h, This function may not be supported depending on the TV model or mobile device.], [1i, The supported functions may differ depending on the version of the SmartThings app.], [1j, You can install the SmartThings app from App Store or Google Play Store.]], [[2a, Managing Mobile Devices.], [2b, Settings General External Device Manager Device Connect Manager Try Now Access Notification Set whether to display a notification when a mobile device attempts to connect to the TV.], [2c, Device List View, edit, or remove a list of mobile devices registered to the TV.]]]\n5                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              [Connection notes for audio devices. For better audio quality, it is a good idea to use an AV receiver. If you connect an external audio device using an optical cable, the Sound Output setting is automatically changed to the connected device. However, to make this happen, you must turn on the external audio device before connecting the optical cable. To manually change the Sound Output setting, do one of the following: Use the Quick Settings screen to change to the connected device: Use the Select button to select Audio Out/Optical on the Sound Output menu. ( Settings directional button Sound Output Use the Settings screen to change to the connected device: Select Audio Out/Optical on the Sound Output menu. ( Settings Sound Sound Output An unusual noise coming from a connected audio device while you are using it may indicate a problem with the audio device itself. If this occurs, ask for assistance from the audio device's manufacturer. Digital audio is only available with 5.1 channel broadcasts. , Connecting with a digital audio (optical) cable. , Audio Input and Output Connections. Make the correct audio connections between your TV and your external devices. For more information about how to select external speakers, refer to]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                [[[0a, Connection notes for audio devices.], [0b, For better audio quality, it is a good idea to use an AV receiver.], [0c, If you connect an external audio device using an optical cable, the Sound Output setting is automatically changed to the connected device.], [0d, However, to make this happen, you must turn on the external audio device before connecting the optical cable.], [0e, To manually change the Sound Output setting, do one of the following: Use the Quick Settings screen to change to the connected device: Use the Select button to select Audio Out/Optical on the Sound Output menu.], [0f, ( Settings directional button Sound Output Use the Settings screen to change to the connected device: Select Audio Out/Optical on the Sound Output menu.], [0g, ( Settings Sound Sound Output An unusual noise coming from a connected audio device while you are using it may indicate a problem with the audio device itself.], [0h, If this occurs, ask for assistance from the audio device's manufacturer.], [0i, Digital audio is only available with 5.1 channel broadcasts.]], [[1a, Connecting with a digital audio (optical) cable.]], [[2a, Audio Input and Output Connections.], [2b, Make the correct audio connections between your TV and your external devices.], [2c, For more information about how to select external speakers, refer to]]]\n6                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [Updating the TV automatically. Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV update its software automatically while you are watching the TV. When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on. If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically. If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off. This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently. This function requires an Internet connection. , Updating the TV automatically. Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV's software update itself automatically while you are watching the TV. When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on. If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically. If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off. This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently. This function requires an Internet connection. , Updating the TV's software to the latest version. DO NOT turn off the TV's power until the update is complete. The TV will turn off and on automatically after completing the software update. Video and audio settings will be reset to their defaults after a software update. Updating through the Internet Settings Support Software Update Update Now Try Now Updating from the Internet requires an active Internet connection. Updating through a USB device Settings Support Software Update Update Now After downloading the update file from the Samsung website and storing it on a USB device, connect the USB device to the TV to update. To update using a USB flash drive, download the update package from Samsung.com to your computer. Then, save the update package in the USB device's top-level folder. Otherwise, the TV will not be able to locate the update package.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   [[[0a, Updating the TV automatically.], [0b, Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV update its software automatically while you are watching the TV.], [0c, When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on.], [0d, If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically.], [0e, If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off.], [0f, This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently.], [0g, This function requires an Internet connection.]], [[1a, Updating the TV automatically.], [1b, Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV's software update itself automatically while you are watching the TV.], [1c, When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on.], [1d, If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically.], [1e, If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off.], [1f, This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently.], [1g, This function requires an Internet connection.]], [[2a, Updating the TV's software to the latest version.], [2b, DO NOT turn off the TV's power until the update is complete.], [2c, The TV will turn off and on automatically after completing the software update.], [2d, Video and audio settings will be reset to their defaults after a software update.], [2e, Updating through the Internet Settings Support Software Update Update Now Try Now Updating from the Internet requires an active Internet connection.], [2f, Updating through a USB device Settings Support Software Update Update Now After downloading the update file from the Samsung website and storing it on a USB device, connect the USB device to the TV to update.], [2g, To update using a USB flash drive, download the update package from Samsung.com to your computer.], [2h, Then, save the update package in the USB device's top-level folder.], [2i, Otherwise, the TV will not be able to locate the update package.]]]\n7                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [Enabling audio for the video description function. Settings General Accessibility Video Description Try Now You can activate an audio guide that provides an audio description of video scenes for the visually impaired. This function is only available with broadcasts that provide this service. , Step by Step instructions to run the options. Turning on Voice Guide Press and hold the VOL button on the remote. The Accessibility Shortcuts menu appears. Press the up or down directional buttons on the remote to move to and highlight the Voice Guide option. Press the Select button on the remote to turn Voice Guide on or off. Close the menu either by pressing on the remote or by pressing the right directional button to highlight Close , and then pressing the Select button.  Turning on Video Description Press and hold the VOL button on the remote. The Accessibility Shortcuts menu appears. Press the up or down directional buttons on the remote to move to and highlight the Video Description option. Press the Select button on the remote to turn Video Description on or off. Close the menu either by pressing on the remote or by pressing the right directional button to highlight Close , and then pressing the Select button. Learning TV Remote Press and hold the VOL button on the remote. The Accessibility Shortcuts menu appears. Press the up or down directional buttons on the remote to move to and highlight the Learn TV Remote option. Press the Select button on the remote. You are now in the e-Manual and specifically on the Learn TV Remote page. Press a button on the remote. The name and function of the button are heard. When you have finished and want to exit the e-Manual, press the button twice to go to the previous page. Accessing the main accessibility menu to change Voice Guide settings You can also go to an accessibility menu from the TV settings menu. This provides more options, for example, to change the speed of Voice Guide. The TV will not verbalize this menu unless Voice Guide is already turned on. Press the button. Press the left directional button until you reach Settings Press Select and a menu will open. Press the down directional button to reach General , and then press Select to open this menu. Use the directional buttons to go to the Accessibility menu, and then press Select to open this menu. The menu will appear with Voice Guide Settings being the first menu. Highlight Voice Guide Settings , and then press Select. A menu appears with the options to change Voice Guide and Volume Speed Pitch Select the menu using the directional buttons, and then press Select. , Enabling voice guides for the visually impaired. Settings General Accessibility Voice Guide Settings Try Now You can activate voice guides that describe the menu options aloud to aid the visually impaired. To activate this function, set Voice Guide . With Voice Guide on, the TV provides voice guides for channel change, volume adjust, information on current and upcoming programs, schedule viewing, other TV functions, and various content in the Internet , and in Search You can go to Voice Guide , and then press the Select button to turn the function on or off. The Voice Guide is provided in the language that is specified on the Language screen. However, some languages are not supported by Voice Guide even though they are listed in the Language screen. English is always supported. For more information about the TV language settings, refer to the menu Changing the volume, speed, and pitch of the Voice Guide You can configure the volume, speed, and pitch of the voice guide.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [[[0a, Enabling audio for the video description function.], [0b, Settings General Accessibility Video Description Try Now You can activate an audio guide that provides an audio description of video scenes for the visually impaired.], [0c, This function is only available with broadcasts that provide this service.]], [[1a, Step by Step instructions to run the options.], [1b, Turning on Voice Guide Press and hold the VOL button on the remote.], [1c, The Accessibility Shortcuts menu appears.], [1d, Press the up or down directional buttons on the remote to move to and highlight the Voice Guide option.], [1e, Press the Select button on the remote to turn Voice Guide on or off.], [1f, Close the menu either by pressing on the remote or by pressing the right directional button to highlight Close , and then pressing the Select button.], [1g, Turning on Video Description Press and hold the VOL button on the remote.], [1h, The Accessibility Shortcuts menu appears.], [1i, Press the up or down directional buttons on the remote to move to and highlight the Video Description option.], [1j, Press the Select button on the remote to turn Video Description on or off.], [1k, Close the menu either by pressing on the remote or by pressing the right directional button to highlight Close , and then pressing the Select button.], [1l, Learning TV Remote Press and hold the VOL button on the remote.], [1m, The Accessibility Shortcuts menu appears.], [1n, Press the up or down directional buttons on the remote to move to and highlight the Learn TV Remote option.], [1o, Press the Select button on the remote.], [1p, You are now in the e-Manual and specifically on the Learn TV Remote page.], [1q, Press a button on the remote.], [1r, The name and function of the button are heard.], [1s, When you have finished and want to exit the e-Manual, press the button twice to go to the previous page.], [1t, Accessing the main accessibility menu to change Voice Guide settings You can also go to an accessibility menu from the TV settings menu.], [1u, This provides more options, for example, to change the speed of Voice Guide.], [1v, The TV will not verbalize this menu unless Voice Guide is already turned on.], [1w, Press the button.], [1x, Press the left directional button until you reach Settings Press Select and a menu will open.], [1y, Press the down directional button to reach General , and then press Select to open this menu.], [1z, Use the directional buttons to go to the Accessibility menu, and then press Select to open this menu.], [1aa, The menu will appear with Voice Guide Settings being the first menu.], [1ab, Highlight Voice Guide Settings , and then press Select.], [1ac, A menu appears with the options to change Voice Guide and Volume Speed Pitch Select the menu using the directional buttons, and then press Select.]], [[2a, Enabling voice guides for the visually impaired.], [2b, Settings General Accessibility Voice Guide Settings Try Now You can activate voice guides that describe the menu options aloud to aid the visually impaired.], [2c, To activate this function, set Voice Guide .], [2d, With Voice Guide on, the TV provides voice guides for channel change, volume adjust, information on current and upcoming programs, schedule viewing, other TV functions, and various content in the Internet , and in Search You can go to Voice Guide , and then press the Select button to turn the function on or off.], [2e, The Voice Guide is provided in the language that is specified on the Language screen.], [2f, However, some languages are not supported by Voice Guide even though they are listed in the Language screen.], [2g, English is always supported.], [2h, For more information about the TV language settings, refer to the menu Changing the volume, speed, and pitch of the Voice Guide You can configure the volume, speed, and pitch of the voice guide.]]]\n8                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [Updating the TV automatically. Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV's software update itself automatically while you are watching the TV. When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on. If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically. If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off. This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently. This function requires an Internet connection. , Updating the TV automatically. Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV update its software automatically while you are watching the TV. When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on. If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically. If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off. This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently. This function requires an Internet connection. , Updating the TV's software to the latest version. DO NOT turn off the TV's power until the update is complete. The TV will turn off and on automatically after completing the software update. Video and audio settings will be reset to their defaults after a software update. Updating through the Internet Settings Support Software Update Update Now Try Now Updating from the Internet requires an active Internet connection. Updating through a USB device Settings Support Software Update Update Now After downloading the update file from the Samsung website and storing it on a USB device, connect the USB device to the TV to update. To update using a USB flash drive, download the update package from Samsung.com to your computer. Then, save the update package in the USB device's top-level folder. Otherwise, the TV will not be able to locate the update package.]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            