TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV's software update itself automatically while you are watching the TV.], [0c, When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on.], [0d, If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically.], [0e, If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off.], [0f, This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently.], [0g, This function requires an Internet connection.]], [[1a, Updating the TV automatically.], [1b, Settings Support Software Update Auto Update Try Now If the TV is connected to the Internet, you can have the TV update its software automatically while you are watching the TV.], [1c, When the background update is completed, it is applied the next time the TV is turned on.], [1d, If you agree to the Smart Hub terms and conditions, Auto Update is set to automatically.], [1e, If you want this function disabled, use the Select button to turn it off.], [1f, This function may take a longer time if another network function is running concurrently.], [1g, This function requires an Internet connection.]], [[2a, Updating the TV's software to the latest version.], [2b, DO NOT turn off the TV's power until the update is complete.], [2c, The TV will turn off and on automatically after completing the software update.], [2d, Video and audio settings will be reset to their defaults after a software update.], [2e, Updating through the Internet Settings Support Software Update Update Now Try Now Updating from the Internet requires an active Internet connection.], [2f, Updating through a USB device Settings Support Software Update Update Now After downloading the update file from the Samsung website and storing it on a USB device, connect the USB device to the TV to update.], [2g, To update using a USB flash drive, download the update package from Samsung.com to your computer.], [2h, Then, save the update package in the USB device's top-level folder.], [2i, Otherwise, the TV will not be able to locate the update package.]]]\n9  [Read Before Using Bixby. Precautions for Bixby The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area. If the language set differs from the language of your country, some features are not available. Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet. Even if the TV is connected to the Internet, there may be no response due to a Bixby server error. The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated. Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone. Symbols including and special characters are not supported. Consequently, if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly. Searched results may not provide complete results. You may be required to pay for some apps. Consequently, you may encounter a service application or contract. To change the current channel by saying channel names as voice commands, you must finish Set Up Your Service Provider . If Set Up Your Service Provider is not completed, you can complete it using the following menu. Settings General Start Setup Try Now To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data. To use the Bixby function, you must: Agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use Agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service. Consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service. Requirements for using Bixby The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise). The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB. , Read Before Using Bixby. Precautions for Bixby The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area. If the language set differs from the language of your country, some features are not available. Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet. Even if the TV is connected to the Internet, there may be no response due to a Bixby server error. The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated. Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone. Symbols including and special characters are not supported. Consequently, if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly. Searched results may not provide complete results. You may be required to pay for some apps. Consequently, you may encounter a service application or contract. To change the current channel by saying channel names as voice commands, you must finish Set Up Your Service Provider . If Set Up Your Service Provider is not completed, you can complete it using the following menu. Settings General Start Setup Try Now To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data. To use the Bixby function, you must: Agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use Agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service. Consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service. Requirements for using Bixby The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise). The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB. , Learning about My Bixby. The image on your TV may differ from the image above depending on the model and geographical area. Samsung Account Go to the Samsung Account screen to create a new account or sign out of your account. If you are signed out of your Samsung account, select Sign In to log in. Settings You can change the voice responses and the voice style of Bixby You can also select a music service provider in the Default music service provider tab. The Default music service provider tab may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area. User information and the experience points (XP) guide You can see user information and the experience points (XP) that you can get from using Bixby You must be signed in to your Samsung account to view the user information and the experience points (XP). This function may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area. Bixby guide You can learn the voice commands that let you use Bixby in various situations. Use the directional buttons to move to the desired command, and then press the Select button. You can operate the TV with various voice commands. To view a tutorial on Bixby , use the directional buttons to move to the bottom, and then select the View Tutorial item. My Bixby ]  [[[0a, Read Before Using Bixby.], [0b, Precautions for Bixby The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area.], [0c, If the language set differs from the language of your country, some features are not available.], [0d, Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet.], [0e, Even if the TV is connected to the Internet, there may be no response due to a Bixby server error.], [0f, The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated.], [0g, Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone.], [0h, Symbols including and special characters are not supported.], [0i, Consequently, if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly.], [0j, Searched results may not provide complete results.], [0k, You may be required to pay for some apps.], [0l, Consequently, you may encounter a service application or contract.], [0m, To change the current channel by saying channel names as voice commands, you must finish Set Up Your Service Provider .], [0n, If Set Up Your Service Provider is not completed, you can complete it using the following menu.], [0o, Settings General Start Setup Try Now To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data.], [0p, To use the Bixby function, you must: Agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use Agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service.], [0q, Consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service.], [0r, Requirements for using Bixby The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise).], [0s, The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB.]], [[1a, Read Before Using Bixby.], [1b, Precautions for Bixby The supported voice interaction languages and features may differ depending on the geographical area.], [1c, If the language set differs from the language of your country, some features are not available.], [1d, Bixby is available only when the TV is connected to the Internet.], [1e, Even if the TV is connected to the Internet, there may be no response due to a Bixby server error.], [1f, The existing functional specifications may be changed if Bixby is updated.], [1g, Bixby is available only on TVs that support it and come with remote controls that have a microphone.], [1h, Symbols including and special characters are not supported.], [1i, Consequently, if a word or sentence contains numeric values or symbols, the function may not operate properly.], [1j, Searched results may not provide complete results.], [1k, You may be required to pay for some apps.], [1l, Consequently, you may encounter a service application or contract.], [1m, To change the current channel by saying channel names as voice commands, you must finish Set Up Your Service Provider .], [1n, If Set Up Your Service Provider is not completed, you can complete it using the following menu.], [1o, Settings General Start Setup Try Now To use the voice text input function and Smart Search function, you must consent to provisions allowing third parties to collect and use your voice data.], [1p, To use the Bixby function, you must: Agree to Smart Hub's Terms of Use Agree to a guidance regarding the collection and use of personal information for the Smart Hub service.], [1q, Consent to the collection and use of personal information for the voice interaction-based service.], [1r, Requirements for using Bixby The voice interaction rate differs with the volume/tone, pronunciation, and ambient sound environment (TV sound and ambient noise).], [1s, The optimal volume for voice commands is between 75 dB and 80 dB.]], [[2a, Learning about My Bixby.], [2b, The image on your TV may differ from the image above depending on the model and geographical area.], [2c, Samsung Account Go to the Samsung Account screen to create a new account or sign out of your account.], [2d, If you are signed out of your Samsung account, select Sign In to log in.], [2e, Settings You can change the voice responses and the voice style of Bixby You can also select a music service provider in the Default music service provider tab.], [2f, The Default music service provider tab may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area.], [2g, User information and the experience points (XP) guide You can see user information and the experience points (XP) that you can get from using Bixby You must be signed in to your Samsung account to view the user information and the experience points (XP).], [2h, This function may not be supported depending on the model or geographical area.], [2i, Bixby guide You can learn the voice commands that let you use Bixby in various situations.], [2j, Use the directional buttons to move to the desired command, and then press the Select button.], [2k, You can operate the TV with various voice commands.], [2l, To view a tutorial on Bixby , use the directional buttons to move to the bottom, and then select the View Tutorial item. My Bixby]]]"}
